.\" Adapted for BNU from the GNU Coreutils 9.11 manual page; see doc/README.md.
.TH RUNCON "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
runcon \- run command with specified security context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runcon
[\fI\,CONTEXT COMMAND \/\fR[\fI\,ARG\/\fR]...]
.br
.B runcon
[\fI\,-c\/\fR] [\fI\,-u USER\/\fR] [\fI\,-r ROLE\/\fR] [\fI\,-t TYPE\/\fR] [\fI\,-l RANGE\/\fR] \fI\,COMMAND \/\fR[\fI\,ARG\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
Run COMMAND with completely-specified CONTEXT, or with current or
transitioned security context modified by one or more of LEVEL,
ROLE, TYPE, and USER.
.PP
If none of \fI-c\fR, \fI-t\fR, \fI-u\fR, \fI-r\fR, or \fI-l\fR, is specified,
the first argument is used as the complete context.  Any additional
arguments after \fICOMMAND\fR are interpreted as arguments to the
command.
.PP
Only carefully-chosen contexts are likely to run successfully.
.PP
Run a program in a different SELinux security context.
With neither CONTEXT nor COMMAND, print the current security context.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
CONTEXT
Complete security context
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#runcon-c'\fB\-c, \-\-compute\fP\X'tty: link'
compute process transition context before modifying
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#runcon-t'\fB\-t, \-\-type=\,TYPE\fP\X'tty: link'\/\fR
type (for same role as parent)
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#runcon-u'\fB\-u, \-\-user=\,USER\fP\X'tty: link'\/\fR
user identity
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#runcon-r'\fB\-r, \-\-role=\,ROLE\fP\X'tty: link'\/\fR
role
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#runcon-l'\fB\-l, \-\-range=\,RANGE\fP\X'tty: link'\/\fR
levelrange
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/runcon#runcon--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/runcon#runcon--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
.SS "Exit status:"
.TP
125
if the runcon command itself fails
.TP
126
if COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked
.TP
127
if COMMAND cannot be found
.TP
\-
the exit status of COMMAND otherwise
